# Docker matches these against the whole path from the context root, and a
# bare `*` never crosses a `/`: `__pycache__/` alone would exclude only a
# top-level one. `**/` makes each rule apply at any depth.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.git/
**/*.pptx
**/*.docx
**/*.xlsx
!supermarket_price_collection.xlsx
**/*.db
.venv/
.claude/
store/
